{# ============================================================================
   THE PRESET COMPONENT — one widget library, for every surface that ships a
   WidgetCatalog. Departments, team, a department's detail and performance tabs,
   an area's zones, a module's dashboard: each includes THIS file with its own
   catalogue and its own routes, and gets the whole component. There are no
   per-surface variations of this pattern, and adding a surface means declaring a
   catalogue and nothing else.

   A MODULE MAY HAVE MORE THAN ONE SURFACE, and then it has ONE library page
   with a section per surface — ruled with the roster's Live plate rail, which
   is a widget surface beside the module's Overview and not a second library.
   Each section carries its own catalogue, its own presets, its own write
   routes and its own CSRF token, because they are separate compositions that
   happen to be configured in one place.

   PARAMETERS — either shape, and the single-surface one is unchanged:

     ONE SURFACE (what every module wrote before this and still writes):
       the parameters listed in @Shell/widget/_library_surface.html.twig,
       passed flat — catalog, builtins, customPresets, active, widgets,
       partial, widgetContext, urls, csrfToken.

     SEVERAL SURFACES:
       surfaces  list of those same parameter bags, one a surface, in the order
                 the page reads. Each may add:
                   label   the section's heading — what this surface IS, in the
                           page's words ("The Live tab's plate rail")
                   intro   one line under it, or nothing
                   anchor  the section's id, so a door elsewhere in the product
                           lands on THIS surface rather than at the top of the
                           page: `…/widgets#rail`. A module with two surfaces
                           has two doors into one page, and a door that always
                           lands at the top is a door that makes the reader
                           hunt for the thing it just opened.

   A SECTION IS THE HOUSE SECTION (`h2.zone` + `p.pgsub`), not furniture of the
   library's own: a reader moving down this page is reading the same page
   grammar they read everywhere else. With one surface no section is drawn at
   all — a heading over the only thing on the page names nothing.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% set _surfaces = surfaces|default(null) %}
{% if _surfaces is null %}
    {{ include('@Shell/widget/_library_surface.html.twig', {
        catalog: catalog,
        builtins: builtins,
        customPresets: customPresets,
        active: active,
        widgets: widgets,
        partial: partial,
        widgetContext: widgetContext,
        urls: urls,
        csrfToken: csrfToken,
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% else %}
    {% for surface in _surfaces %}
        <section class="w-surface"{% if surface.anchor is defined and surface.anchor %} id="{{ surface.anchor }}"{% endif %}>
            {% if surface.label is defined and surface.label %}
                <h2 class="zone">{{ surface.label }}</h2>
            {% endif %}
            {% if surface.intro is defined and surface.intro %}
                <p class="pgsub">{{ surface.intro }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            {{ include('@Shell/widget/_library_surface.html.twig', {
                catalog: surface.catalog,
                builtins: surface.builtins,
                customPresets: surface.customPresets,
                active: surface.active,
                widgets: surface.widgets,
                partial: surface.partial,
                widgetContext: surface.widgetContext,
                urls: surface.urls,
                csrfToken: surface.csrfToken,
            }, with_context: false) }}
        </section>
    {% endfor %}
{% endif %}
